{"step_index":56,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T08:08:14Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nFor just the above questions, which one of them requires a diagram and what is the diagram? Give me a prompt so I can generate it. Don't generate. And these are the potions for your reference.         Question: Explain various casting defects with causes and remedies.\r\n\r\nAnswer (Write 5-6 for 7M):\r\n\r\nBLOW HOLES Cause: Moisture in sand, low permeability, excessive gas generation. Remedy: Use dry sand. Improve venting. Increase permeability of moulding sand.\r\n\r\nMISRUN (Incomplete filling) Cause: Pouring temperature too low, thin sections in casting, improper gating. Remedy: Increase pouring temperature. Redesign gating system to ensure proper flow.\r\n\r\nSHRINKAGE CAVITY Cause: Insufficient molten metal to feed the casting during solidification. No riser or riser is too small. Remedy: Use adequately sized risers. Place risers at the last point to solidify (hot spot).\r\n\r\nHOT TEARS (Hot Cracks) Cause: The casting cannot shrink freely because the mould or core is too rigid (poor collapsibility). Remedy: Improve collapsibility of sand. Add proper fillets at corners. Avoid sharp changes in section thickness.\r\n\r\nCOLD SHUT Cause: Two streams of molten metal meet but do not fuse because they have cooled too much. Remedy: Increase pouring temperature. Pour faster. Redesign gating to avoid divided flow.\r\n\r\nMETAL PENETRATION Cause: Sand grains are too coarse. Molten metal seeps between sand particles. Remedy: Use finer sand. Apply mould wash/coating on the cavity surface.\r\n\r\nWARPAGE / DISTORTION Cause: Uneven cooling of different sections of the casting. Remedy: Design uniform wall thickness. Use distortion allowance in pattern.\r\n\r\nGATING SYSTEM ELEMENTS (3-4 Marks) Asked: 5/9 papers (Borderline)\r\nQuestion: Explain the elements of a gating system with a sketch.\r\n\r\nAnswer:\r\n\r\nA gating system is the network of channels that delivers molten metal from the ladle to the mould cavity.\r\n\r\nELEMENTS (in order of metal flow):\r\n\r\nPOURING BASIN: A funnel-shaped cup at the top where molten metal is first poured. Reduces turbulence and prevents slag from entering.\r\nSPRUE: A vertical tapered channel that carries metal downward from the pouring basin. Tapered (narrow at bottom) to prevent air aspiration.\r\nSPRUE WELL: A small reservoir at the base of the sprue. Absorbs the kinetic energy of falling metal and reduces turbulence.\r\nRUNNER: A horizontal channel at the parting line that distributes metal from the sprue to the gates.\r\nGATE (INGATE): The final opening through which metal enters the mould cavity. Controls the flow rate and direction of metal entry.\r\nRISER: A reservoir of molten metal connected to the casting. Feeds extra metal to compensate for shrinkage during solidification. Last to solidify.\r\nDiagram: Draw a cross-section of a mould showing all 6 elements connected in sequence from top to bottom. Label each clearly.\r\n\r\nCASTING DEFECTS WITH CAUSES AND REMEDIES: Question: Explain various casting defects with causes and remedies. Answer (Write 5-6 for 7M): • BLOW HOLES: Cause: Moisture in sand, low permeability, excessive gas generation. Remedy: Use dry sand. Improve venting. Increase permeability of moulding sand. • MISRUN (Incomplete filling): Cause: Pouring temperature too low, thin sections in casting, improper gating. Remedy: Increase pouring temperature. Redesign gating system to ensure proper flow. • SHRINKAGE CAVITY: Cause: Insufficient molten metal to feed the casting during solidification. No riser or riser is too small. Remedy: Use adequately sized risers. Place risers at the last point to solidify (hot spot). • HOT TEARS (Hot Cracks): Cause: The casting cannot shrink freely because the mould or core is too rigid (poor collapsibility). Remedy: Improve collapsibility of sand. Add proper fillets at corners. Avoid sharp changes in section thickness. • COLD SHUT: Cause: Two streams of molten metal meet but do not fuse because they have cooled too much. Remedy: Increase pouring temperature. Pour faster. Redesign gating to avoid divided flow. • METAL PENETRATION: Cause: Sand grains are too coarse. Molten metal seeps between sand particles. Remedy: Use finer sand. Apply mould wash/coating on the cavity surface. • WARPAGE / DISTORTION: Cause: Uneven cooling of different sections of the casting. Remedy: Design uniform wall thickness. Use distortion allowance in pattern.\r\n\r\nGATING SYSTEM ELEMENTS (3-4 Marks) Asked: 5/9 papers (Borderline): Question: Explain the elements of a gating system with a sketch. Answer: A gating system is the network of channels that delivers molten metal from the ladle to the mould cavity. ELEMENTS (in order of metal flow): • POURING BASIN: A funnel-shaped cup at the top where molten metal is first poured. Reduces turbulence and prevents slag from entering. • SPRUE: A vertical tapered channel that carries metal downward from the pouring basin. Tapered (narrow at bottom) to prevent air aspiration. • SPRUE WELL: A small reservoir at the base of the sprue. Absorbs the kinetic energy of falling metal and reduces turbulence. • RUNNER: A horizontal channel at the parting line that distributes metal from the sprue to the gates. • GATE (INGATE): The final opening through which metal enters the mould cavity. Controls the flow rate and direction of metal entry. • RISER: A reservoir of molten metal connected to the casting. Feeds extra metal to compensate for shrinkage during solidification. Last to solidify. • Diagram: Draw a cross-section of a mould showing all 6 elements connected in sequence from top to bottom. Label each clearly.\r\n\r\n1:28 PM\r\nQuestion: Explain the properties of moulding sand.\r\n\r\nAnswer (Write 6-7 properties for 7M, any 4 for 4M):\r\n\r\nPermeability: The ability of moulding sand to allow gases and steam to pass through it during pouring. If permeability 